{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Jacob went out, etc.</b> The reason the verse was not satisfied with informing us of his journey in the previous passage, where it is written (Genesis 28:7) ״וַיִּשְׁמַע יַעֲקֹב, etc., וַיֵּלֶךְ״ etc., is to inform us that he encountered something on the way before reaching his destination, and since the matter was interrupted, it returned to say ״וַיֵּצֵא״ etc. But we need to know why it was necessary to say <b>and he went</b> etc. — and all the more so since his encounter at the Place happened before he reached Haran, so it should not have preceded what came later. Further, why does it say <b>חָרָנָה</b> (with the directional heh) and not simply לְחָרָן? And even though they of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 68) ״every word״ etc. — with all this, the verse intends something by changing the form in various places." "<b>Indeed,</b> the Torah intends to set forth in order everything that befell Jacob from the time of his departure. And this is the beginning of the matter: <b>And Jacob went out</b> etc. — meaning: he did nothing but depart, and had no need to walk on foot; and the one walking was חָרָנָה — that is, it is what it says: <b>and he went חָרָנָה</b>, meaning: חָרָנָה, it went forth from its place to meet Jacob face to face." "<b>Further,</b> it alludes to inform us that when Jacob went out from Be'er-Sheva, the wrath of Esav departed immediately, and this is what it says: <b>and he went חָרָנָה</b> — the wrath (חֵרוֹן) of Esav departed." "And according to their words of blessed memory, that Esav sent Elifaz after him etc., it further intends in saying <b>and he went חָרָנָה</b> to allude to the going of Elifaz after him בְּחָרוֹן (in wrath). And perhaps it is for this reason that the verse then says ״וַיִּפְגַּע בַמָּקוֹם״ to allude that he saw himself in distress and was in need of prayer:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:16.485843051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}